# Translation Review Needed

The following files contain machine-assisted translations that should be
reviewed by native speakers before production use.

## Files requiring review

### Turkish (tr)
- `src/i18n/locales/tr.json` — UI strings (150+ keys)
- `src/i18n/data-translations/tr.json` — Budget category names (~90 keys)
- `src/data/descriptionData.tr.ts` — Topic tooltip descriptions (~90 entries)

### English (en)
- `src/i18n/locales/en.json` — UI strings (150+ keys)
- `src/i18n/data-translations/en.json` — Budget category names (~90 keys)
- `src/data/descriptionData.en.ts` — Topic tooltip descriptions (~90 entries)

## Notes for reviewers

- Budget category names (hauptfunktions_bezeichnung, etc.) are official German
  administrative terms. Translations should be accurate but accessible.
- The FAQ content is conversational German. Translations should sound natural,
  not literal.
- Turkish translations are particularly challenging due to the specialized
  budget/administrative vocabulary.
- Key terms to verify:
  - "Doppelhaushalt" → "biennial budget" (EN) / "iki yıllık bütçe" (TR)
  - "Haushaltsplan" → "budget plan" (EN) / "bütçe planı" (TR)
  - "Einzelplan" → "sectoral budget" (EN) / "sektörel bütçe" (TR)
  - "Titel" → "budget item" (EN) / "bütçe kalemi" (TR)
  - "Funktionen" vs "Bereiche" — these are the two sorting modes
  - "Gesamtausgaben" / "Gesamteinnahmen" — root treemap labels
  - "Höchste Ausgabetitel" / "Höchste Einnahmetitel" — list section headers
